Just for a contrary voice...

Gehennom doesn't seem nearly as bad to me as it does to others around
here. Maybe it's just because I haven't gotten down to Gehennom *that*
often (I have 5 or 6 ascensions, with maybe 3 deaths post-castle).
Being able to "run" with a mouse click takes a lot of the tediousness
out of actually traversing the mazes. It's also helpful if you don't
feel that you have to actually work your way through every bit of
maze, once you know where the stairs are.

Have you tried the Heck2 patch? It at least swaps out various special
levels, so you don't know which one you're getting all the time; plus,
the special levels use up some dungeon levels that would otherwise be
used up by mazes.

The "I'm an unkillable machine" issue is still there, but that's
largely caused by players massively overpreparing by the time they hit
the Castle. Short of having more elements (resistances, perhaps) that
are needed in Gehennom and only obtainable in Gehennom, there is
little to get in the way of the determined player deciding to become a
walking tank by the point of the Castle.

